From 1271749d131fdfbce66d854e7d8050db9919ceaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kamil Monicz <kamil@monicz.dev>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:27:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Accept scalar buffers with null shape and strides

Zero-dimensional buffers represent one scalar and legitimately provide no shape or stride arrays. Require those arrays only for nonzero dimensions, and return empty metadata slices without constructing Rust slices from null pointers. Cover typed acquisition, C and Fortran copies, scalar pointers, and exactly-once explicit or automatic release.
